<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muzaffar Shah of Malacca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1459</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muzaffar Shah was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> from about 1445 to 1459, the first of its rulers to use the title sultan. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> the state religion, and with his bendahara <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tun-perak">Tun Perak</a> he repelled Siamese attacks and extended Malacca's power over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>. Under his son Mansur Shah the sultanate reached its peak.</p></div>
